This is a game demo about programming and space exploration.

This uses SDL alongside with the companion libraries of SDL_ttf, SDL_image and SDL_mixer.
They are included as git submodules under the vendor/ folder.

This is a standard cmake project and you can generate build files with:
```bash
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
```

By default the executable will go into build/bin/ or build/bin/$ConfigurationName depending on the compiler.
The application will search for assets and a file named run_tree.txt listing what it needs to load in the folder the executable is located in.
The application needs shaders to function and they are kept in source format in version control.
So you need to create an asset/shader/binary/ folder and put the compiled binary forms of the shaders in asset/shader/src/.
There is a python script asset/shader/compile_shaders.py that can automatically compile and put shaders you want.
You need directx shader compiler installed to use it.

You need to copy the asset/ folder and run_tree.txt file at the top level of the repository to where the executable is located in.
